{"type":"message","id":"77ececb4","parentId":"94b92577","timestamp":"2026-05-20T12:02:24.396Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Cloudflare Workers error 1101 is typically \"Worker Not Found\" or \"Worker Execution Failed\" - meaning the worker itself might have an unhandled error or the route doesn't exist. Let me try a different approach and just check the platform status with a simple ping or health check.\n\nActually, wait - looking at the error more carefully, \"1101\" from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker threw an exception\" or \"Worker not found\". This suggests the API might have a bug or the /send endpoint doesn't work as expected.\n\nLet me try to understand what's happening with a simpler request, and maybe try different endpoint formats.\n\nActually, looking at the history endpoint format, it was GET /history?threadId=arbitration&limit=5. And the history works! So the GET endpoint is working but the POST /send might not be implemented correctly.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2ddc7e80-b1b3-4ae9-bbcf-4a31999345fd","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-4a82ebba-7e6f-49b2-9d6e-4efc341bfc69","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n  -d \"threadId=arbitration&content=test\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":323,"output":320,"cacheRead":18512,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19155,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779278533524,"responseId":"chatcmpl-5192d95a-4921-440d-883a-be